5. SIMULTANEOUS OPERATION (solar at the window, a vehicle at 24 V, the full load, charging)
   the front end's input is the H3 line's at VIN_RAW whatever the sources share: at 24 V at most 4.194 A, 65.9 % of the breaker's lowest 6.364 A; the tracker's
   ceiling (28.28 V minimum) is above 24 V, so the panel carries the bus first and the vehicle supplies only what the panel does not give
   delivered at VBAT: 84.5 to 99.6 W (U3 between its minimum at the lowest bus and its board-current maximum at the bus's top, U3 0.9733)
   PS-IDLE-SPEC plan                    42.8 W: carried by the sources, up to 41.7 W left to charge (at most 3 A ChargeCurrent)
   PS-TYP plus USB-C plan              112.3 W: the pack supplies at least 27.8 W, 1.93 A at a 14.4 V stack; no charge
   the PA keyed alone at 113 W, plan   162.3 W: the pack supplies at least 77.8 W, 5.4 A at a 14.4 V stack; no charge
   PS-ALLTX plan                       203.8 W: the pack supplies at least 119.3 W, 8.28 A at a 14.4 V stack; no charge
   PS-ALLTX high                         272 W: the pack supplies at least 187.5 W, 13.02 A at a 14.4 V stack; no charge
   no stage is pushed past its limit: the entry stays under its breaker's lowest (H3), R11 carries at most 4.964 A, every can at most 2.4096 A, the pack's
   current falls by what the sources give (PS-ALLTX's floors of D-11 hold as on the pack alone), and the outlets drop while the PA keys
   per source at VBAT, L4-E11's envelope at the plug (the losses hot, the corrected knee): 9 V 29.09 to 42.52 W; 12 V 32.22 to 47.72 W; 24 V 69.97 to 90.81 W;
     36 V 84.55 to 99.64 W (round 2's figures at VIN_RAW with no loss and L4-E5's drawn knee: 9 V 19.9 to 36.6 W, 12 V up to 47.4 W, 24 V up to 90.6 W)
   so at a 9.00 V plug the vehicle runs PS-IDLE-SPEC (42.8 W) with the pack supplementing, and charges only while the kit draws under 29.09 W

6. STARTUP
   source arriving: the selected entry (L4-E11) turns on at 8.44 V of DC_P at the most and slews the bus up (0.382 to 1.219 A for at most 2.5 ms; the drawn
     LM5069, R21 '38.3k 1% (UVLO: 9 V)', cannot start from a 9.00 V plug); U3 is in HIZ below 7.378 V (certain, the corrected knee; 8.466 V on L4-E5's drawn line); the H3 line
     bounds U3 from its first cycle with no host; the panel: the stage's own UVLO and soft start, the hold at 17.593 V; SWEN stays off while
     TRK_LDO33 is under 2.662 V, whatever the ramp (L4-E7R), and each backstop trip restarts through the soft start
   source leaving: VBAT is the system node with no battery FET, so the pack carries the loads without a break; IIN_HOST resets to 3.25 A
     and firmware writes 4.7 A again (FW-A16 restated); VIN_RAW falls through the restart guard (7.139 V at the highest with R14 76.8k; 8.31 V as drawn)
     and the front end stops
   SOURCE-ONLY AND DEAD-PACK OPERATION (the focused check's B4; U-04)
     what the maker's sheet establishes (SLUSE66A): after VBUS qualification 'Converter powers up' (9.3.1), with no battery condition, and its power-up
       figures are drawn '2-cell without battery' (Figures 10-4, 10-5): U3 supplies VSYS with no battery; DPM gives the system priority and, past the input's
       limit, 'the system voltage starts to drop' (9.3.17); below VSYS_MIN the charge is clamped at 384 mA (9.6.2.1). Board A straps
       CELL_BATPRESZ for 4S (R26/R27), so U3 never sees 'battery removal': with the pack absent it regulates VBAT at ChargeVoltage, at most 16.884 V
       (INFERRED: no current in R17, so the voltage loop sets VSRN); with the pack's discharge FET open at CUV it charges through that FET's
       body diode at the clamp, and VBAT sits at the pack's 10 V or so plus the diode (INFERRED), against the converters' assumed 10 V floor (A-14)
     the source envelope with no usable pack (round 2, at VIN_RAW with no loss; L4-E11's at the plug in section 5): 9 V 19.9 to 36.6 W, 12 V up to 47.4 W, 24 V up to 90.6 W, against PS-IDLE-SPEC
       42.8 W: at 9 V the kit cannot run its profile on the source alone (it sheds or stops); at 12 V and 24 V the line's maximum is above it
       (no minimum is printed there, so CONDITIONAL on the charger's limit tolerance); before the host writes
       IIN_HOST the input limit gives about 1.6 to 1.7 A at the 20 V bus, about 31 W into VSYS (CHARGER-STATE-SEQUENCE.md, INFERRED), so the boot load must stay under it until FW-A16, which
       FW-C01's order (the charger before any slot) intends but no record measures
     not resolvable from the held documents in round 2: whether the converter keeps VSYS up with charge inhibited and no battery FET (Q-TI-3,
       prepared in REVIEW-REQUEST.md, not sent); whether the gauge lets a pack at or below CUV take charge through its FETs with no precharge FET; whether every load
       converter runs at the dead pack's VBAT (A-14). Board E's always-on comes up on CELL_F from VBAT
     L4-E11 (accepted) selects arrangement (A), the drawn charger with rules R-a to R-d (the holds as a state table, R-b's two charge settings,
       the shedding sequence, the image's pre-charge); at a 9.00 V plug the shed warm-up (28.12 W plan) is carried with 0.98 W in hand while P1 stays
       at most 20.51 W; REQ-015 at 9.00 V at the plug is a CONDITIONAL CANDIDATE (E11-05, E11-06, E11-09, E11-22, E11-23): U-04 stays an unresolved
       choice until that evidence lands (section 12d)

7. FAULTS, TRACED ACROSS THE STAGES
   reversed vehicle input (REQ-015): DC_P is back-fed from VIN_RAW through Q7's body diode (L4-E5's finding), so Q1 holds DC_P plus the
     reversed input: 51.56 V with the drawn ceiling, 66.15 V with L4-E5's raised ceiling, against BSC039N06NS 60 V; a CSD19532Q5B (100 V) holds it,
     and U3's cathode to anode stays under its 70 V recommended and 75 V absolute
   a short behind F1: F1 must interrupt at up to 43.18 V (the basis L4-E11 keeps; the selected OV maximum 41.22 V); the drawn cable (2 m of 1 mm2 a way)
     and lead (500 mm of AWG 18)
     give 0.0899 Ohm at 20 C and 0.0758 Ohm at -20 C, so a stiff source drives at most 569.8 A (copper alone); the drawn 297 is rated 32 V DC: NOT MET
     as drawn; the selected 0997010.WXN is rated 58 V DC and 1000 A at 58 V DC: MEETS (part A, section 11); the selected interconnect (D-06) is
     specified by its loop's floor, 56.93 mOhm at 20 C, so a stiff source drives at most 900 A (L4-E11 6; the construction 871 A): MEETS, CONDITIONAL
     on the four-wire acceptance (E11-11)
   VBUS20 shorted: the front end holds the output at 4.57 A at 9 V (R12) and 7.262 A above 14 V (R11 8 mOhm); VIN_RAW then carries at most 11.65 A;
     the vehicle entry's breaker opens on overcurrent (6.364 to 7.136 A) after 0.247 to 0.49 ms, or on its filtered short-circuit sense (10.36 to 13.87 A), and
     retries every 0.5 s (the drawn LM5069 limited at 4.85 to 6.15 A for 3.13 to 8.16 ms); the panel's stage regulates at 2.9318 A at most and its backstop trips
     at 3.7408 A at most (SWEN, inside 1.087 ms); the restart guard cycles the front end
   VBAT shorted: the pack's SCD (60 A in 0.2 ms), OCD2, the 25 A blades and F2 against 240 to 480 A prospective; U3 at its input limit
   the pack's charge FET opening mid-charge (a designed event, REQ-046): VBAT is held at ChargeVoltage (16.884 V at most), BATOVP stops switching
     at 17.64 V, SYSOVP at 20 V; L2's energy at the stop, 0.1341 mJ (peak 6.896 A, L +20 %), into VBAT's 34 capacitors (248.2 uF nominal, 49.64 uF kept at 0.2)
     ends at 20.135 V from the SYSOVP maximum, under the TPS2596's 21 V; 6.54 uF would do (0.0264 of the nominal)
   U2 failed (Q2 short or FB open) and U3 lost, a single fault: s120 section 11 and S-111 carry it with its options; this record claims no
     exemption for it (ASM-001 is the LoRa and cellular exception; R-48's decision stays an engineering one, open) and the
     options (an SMCJ22A on VBUS20: VR 22 V over the 20.96 V band; an independent over-voltage trip)
   PoE monitor (HF-F02): U17's inputs at 54 V against the INA226's 40 V absolute: NOT MET as drawn; on R227, 5 mOhm in the stage's input
     (part A): 3.682 A at a 10 V stack, 18.59 mV; 14.33 A at the stage's fault bound, 72.38 mV, against 81.92 mV full scale; common mode at most 20.135 V
   the solar entry (L4-E7R): CS101 keeps the input at 27.82 V under D4's 28 V standoff; the capability scenario holds TRK_VS at 44.25 V and PV_P at 44.74 V;
     a reversed panel conducts through D4 (DECISION-31 E-N1); the LT8705A's single faults are layer 8's list (a shorted INB filter capacitor
     defeats the backstop); under CS101 the filtered ripple, 0.0585 A, stays under the 0.113 A margin (D-01, resolved in design, CONDITIONAL on the loop's
     typical rows)
   the vehicle entry under CS101 (M2) at REQ-015's 36 V: 38.83 V against the drawn OVLO minimum 37.78 V (NOT MET as drawn), the selected OV minimum 39.6 V:
     MEETS (the alternative's 39.71 V likewise)
   a hot short behind the selected entry: the breaker's short-circuit trip; at the start every fault inside Q7's derated chart; in service the
     peak OPEN on the loop's inductance (E11-20); F1's I2t at most 6.7311 A2s, 7.24 % of its typical melting I2t (section 12a)

