   H2 PS-IDLE-SPEC with the tablet's window (M2): 44.80 W; the line: as H1; +20.8 K at the binding line; C1 above 29.2 C ambient; on the conservative bound: 62 to 75 K over the bound's one-node lid-open points (0.598 to 0.720 W/K; INFERRED, computed at smaller rises); with the heat-rejection approaches: not computed: L4-E12 15 takes the profile's heat alone: the window adds 1.4 W, so the +70 C class at +40 C needs 1.493 W/K, over the combined route's 1.384 W/K at the profile's heat (INFERRED)
   H3 E3-O, the heat stage with the ballasts (M3): 27.09 W; the line: +70 C class at +55 C: 1.806 W/K; 67.55 C at the binding line (L4-E12); on the conservative bound: the air 92.61 C (0.720 W/K at 37.6 K); with every session measure 0.691 against the 0.903 W/K the module's +85 C intake needs: a gap of 0.212 W/K (L4-E12 9d); with the heat-rejection approaches: not computed: L4-E12 15 takes the profile's heat alone; E3-O's own options are L4-E12 9e's
   H4 E5 under the hold, with the ballasts (M4): 21.59 W; the line: +70 C class at +60 C: 2.159 W/K, the BINDING line; 70.00 C at the line; T-H1 passes at a reading of at least 2.416 W/K (its expanded uncertainty deducted); on the conservative bound: the air 90.93 C (0.698 W/K at 30.9 K), 83.41 C with F3; with every session measure 0.671 against the 0.621 W/K needed: it holds (L4-E12 9d); with the heat-rejection approaches: not computed: L4-E12 15 takes the profile's heat alone; E5 holds on the bound with every session measure
