   R25 the approved profile's heat into the case: 43.4 (l4e12_thermal.out: this record's figure at a0212d9e, as L4-E12 10a quotes it); 43.413 (l4e12_thermal.out: L4-E12 10a: 42.824 W at the pack plus the pack's own I2R)
      kept: 43.4 W in this record's tables; 43.413 W in L4-E12's thresholds; why: one quantity at two roundings; 1.447 W/K either way
16e NORMAL OPERATION IN THE IN-USE ENVELOPE (REQ-024's top), against L4-E12's conservative bound, the combined route and T-H1's thresholds at the profile's heat (INFERRED, one node, the cells at the inside air)
   N1 the approved profile PS-IDLE-SPEC, lid open: 43.40 W; the inside air at the top on the bound 100.3 to 112.6 C (0.720 to 0.598 W/K); the conductance each limit needs there: C1's inside-air trigger 4.340 W/K; the cells' charge start (T3) 21.700 W/K; the +70 C class 1.447 W/K; the module's intake 0.964 W/K; past C1's inside-air trigger, the cells' charge start (T3), the +70 C class, the module's intake
   N2 the profile with a charge running on shore, lid open: 46.85 W; the inside air at the top on the bound 105.1 to 118.3 C (0.720 to 0.598 W/K); the conductance each limit needs there: C1's inside-air trigger 4.685 W/K; the cells' charge start (T3) 23.423 W/K; the +70 C class 1.562 W/K; the module's intake 1.041 W/K; past C1's inside-air trigger, the cells' charge start (T3), the +70 C class, the module's intake
   N3 the heat stage on shore with the ballasts (C1's shed state; E3-L, LO-01a), lid open: 27.09 W; the inside air at the top on the bound 77.6 to 85.3 C (0.720 to 0.598 W/K); the conductance each limit needs there: C1's inside-air trigger 2.709 W/K; the cells' charge start (T3) 13.543 W/K; the +70 C class 0.903 W/K; the module's intake 0.602 W/K; past C1's inside-air trigger, the cells' charge start (T3), the +70 C class
   N4 the heat stage on shore with the ballasts, lid closed: 27.09 W; the inside air at the top on the bound 91.7 C (0.524 W/K); the conductance each limit needs there: C1's inside-air trigger 2.709 W/K; the cells' charge start (T3) 13.543 W/K; the +70 C class 0.903 W/K; the module's intake 0.602 W/K; past C1's inside-air trigger, the cells' charge start (T3), the +70 C class, the module's intake
   N5 the reduced mode PS-RED (D-02b's lid-closed state), lid closed: 22.40 W; the inside air at the top on the bound 82.7 C (0.524 W/K); the conductance each limit needs there: C1's inside-air trigger 2.240 W/K; the cells' charge start (T3) 11.200 W/K; the +70 C class 0.747 W/K; the module's intake 0.498 W/K; past C1's inside-air trigger, the cells' charge start (T3), the +70 C class
   the profile's ceilings (the highest ambient at which each limit holds), by conductance: on the bound, one node (0.598 to 0.720 W/K); on the bound at the profile's heat, two nodes (0.767 W/K); the combined route on the bound (1.384 W/K); a reading at the profile's heat of 1.509 W/K (1.447 W/K after its uncertainty); a reading at the profile's heat of 1.575 W/K (1.507 W/K after its uncertainty); a reading at the profile's heat of 1.930 W/K (1.832 W/K after its uncertainty); the outside films' cap (1.540 to 1.571 W/K)
     C1's inside-air trigger (+50 C): -22.6 to -10.3 C | -6.6 C | 18.6 C | 20.0 C | 21.2 C | 26.3 C | 21.8 to 22.4 C
     the cells' charge start (T3) (+42 C): -30.6 to -18.3 C | -14.6 C | 10.6 C | 12.0 C | 13.2 C | 18.3 C | 13.8 to 14.4 C
     the +70 C class (+70 C): -2.6 to 9.7 C | 13.4 C | 38.6 C | 40.0 C | 41.2 C | 46.3 C | 41.8 to 42.4 C
     the module's intake (+85 C): 12.4 to 24.7 C | 28.4 C | 53.6 C | 55.0 C | 56.2 C | 61.3 C | 56.8 to 57.4 C
   The approved profile is not thermally feasible on the conservative bound in the upper part of the envelope: on the bound (0.598 to 0.720 W/K lid open, one node, the fans' flow at zero) its 43.4 W put the inside air 60 to 73 K over the ambient, so it keeps the +70 C class only below about -3 to 10 C ambient and the module's +85 C intake below about 12 to 25 C (INFERRED); L4-E12's two-node model at the profile's own heat gives 0.767 W/K, the air 96.61 C at +40 C, the +70 C class only below about 13 C.
   It is feasible across the in-use envelope only above a T-H1 reading: at REQ-024's +40 C its +70 C class needs 1.447 W/K lid open with the fans (the module's intake 0.964 W/K), only 0.093 to 0.124 W/K under the outside films' cap; T-H1's point at the profile's heat reads it directly, at a reading of at least 1.509 W/K (L4-E12 10e). That reading is the deciding fact for the architecture (U-02). Under it no route inside the rulings restores the profile on the bound: L4-E12's best, the large loads led into the plate with fins and the open lid as a second radiator, reaches 1.384 W/K, 1.252 W (0.063 W/K) short; it is built and read at the same point (R-170 to R-172), and if it still reads short the owner's options are an alternative duty cycle at +40 C, labelled (PS-IDLE, 40.242 W, under the route's 42.161 W by 1.919 W), or a requirement change. No reading keeps the profile under C1's +50 C trigger at +40 C (it needs 4.34 W/K, over the cap): there the kit runs C1's shed states by design (CONOPS 4), and the heat stage then needs 0.903 W/K lid open for the +70 C class, which the 0.951 W/K band at E5's hold (0.903 W/K after its uncertainty) covers.
   Charging in normal operation: the cells accept charge at or under the gauge's 42 C start. With the profile running that holds on the bound only below -30.6 C ambient (L4-E10), at the outside films' cap only below about 13.8 to 14.4 C, and at no reading at +40 C (it needs 21.7 W/K). On SC-37's September day (the air 13.2 to 18.3 C) the pack accepts charge with the profile running only if the case conducts 1.51 to 1.83 W/K, the warm end over the cap; T-H1's point at the profile's heat reads it (at least 1.575 and 1.930 W/K), and the combined route reaches 1.355 to 1.360 W/K on the bound, 0.153 and 0.472 W/K short. The solar-assisted rows of 2b assume a charge the sealed case may not admit, so their solar part is CONDITIONAL on T-H1 (INFERRED; the battery-only rows are not, since a battery-only run, 2.52 h, is short against the case's 4.57 h time constant on the bound).
   Electrical feasibility is a separate question (1d, 8a): every interface row MEETS or is CONDITIONAL with no defect open. Thermal feasibility in normal operation is U-02's, decided by T-H1's lid-open, fans-on reading against the conductances above.

