20. THE EXIT STATEMENT (the owner's definition, quoted; each U on this record's reading, the consolidation's results integrated)
   The precise bounded question (U-02): does the sealed Peli 1450, lid open with the fans at full duty, conduct at least 1.447 W/K at the approved profile's heat? That is what the profile's +70 C class needs at REQ-024's +40 C (43.413 W into the case over 30 K; its module's +85 C intake 0.964 W/K); charging with the profile running on SC-37's design day (the air 13.2 to 18.3 C) needs 1.507 to 1.832 W/K. Below, L4-E12's conservative bound gives 0.767 W/K at the profile's heat, the fans' inside film credited at zero; above, no inside film passes the outside films' cap (1.540 to 1.571 W/K at E5's and E3-O's smaller rises). No held document bounds the fans' inside film, so a reading decides it; missing evidence is not proof of a shortfall.
   Its executable resolution path. (1) T-H1's point at the profile's heat, P1 (R-104, Layer 9's bench; the owner authorises it, OW-8): lid open; the fans at full duty (the two mixers and slot 3's cooler, stand-ins until D-18); two heaters, 42.4 W, spread as the boards dissipate; room air, still; eight channels on one logger (four mixed air, two ambient, the plate's and a wall's inner faces); run until the mixed air drifts at most 0.1 K/h over an hour (5.9 to 21.1 h); G = P / rise. (2) A reading of at least 1.509 W/K: the profile works at +40 C with no route; at least 1.575 W/K: charging with it on the design day's cold end; at least 1.930 W/K: on its warm end. (3) Under 1.509 W/K: build the combined route, the large loads (23.641 W) led into the plate with fins on its free strips and the open lid as a second radiator (R-170 to R-172; passive: no power, no endurance change), and read it at the same point; on the bound it reaches 1.384 W/K, 1.252 W (0.063 W/K) short. (4) If it still reads under 1.509 W/K, the owner's options: an ALTERNATIVE duty cycle at +40 C, labelled as such (PS-IDLE, the monitor dimmed and no beacon: 40.242 W into the case, under the route's 42.161 W by 1.919 W; nothing fits on the bound alone), or a requirement change (the profile's ambient ceiling, or charging with the profile running on the design day). (5) Then the point at E5's hold, P2 (21.2 W), and the remaining points (the lid-closed state, the fans off, the fractions; R-151).
   The two points' readings, both kept (each the target plus its expanded uncertainty at that point's rise). At P1, the profile's 42.4 W: 1.509 W/K meets 1.447 W/K (the profile at +40 C, the +70 C class, no route); 1.575 W/K meets 1.507 W/K (charging with the profile on the design day's cold end); 1.930 W/K meets 1.832 W/K (charging with the profile on the design day's warm end). At P2, E5's hold's 21.2 W: 2.462 W/K meets 2.159 W/K (E5's line, the design as stated); 1.516 W/K meets 1.399 W/K (E3-O with F4, the connectors in the exhaust); 1.410 W/K meets 1.309 W/K (E3-O with F4, the connectors out of the exhaust); 1.199 W/K meets 1.125 W/K (E5 with F4 and F3); 0.951 W/K meets 0.903 W/K (E3-O with every session measure); 0.644 W/K meets 0.621 W/K (E5 with every session measure); under 0.951 W/K the owner decides (a deviation of E3-O or a device-set re-pick). P1 supersedes the 21.2 W bands for the profile, which they read only between 1.516 and 2.462 W/K; P2's bands still decide E5's and E3-O's lines, since the conductance grows with the rise and a reading at P1's larger rise overstates it at P2's.
